    "name": "CourseMaster Backend API",
    "description": "CourseMaster Backend API collection.\n\nBase URL: {{baseUrl}} (default http://localhost:5000)\nAuth: Bearer JWT. Collection requests use {{token}}; admin folders use {{adminToken}}.\n\nSeeded accounts:\n- Admin: admin@coursemaster.com / admin123\n- Student: student@coursemaster.com / student123\n\nQuick start:\n1. Start the API (npm run dev) and seed data (npm run seed).\n2. Run \"Auth > Login (Student)\" to populate {{token}} and {{userId}}.\n3. Run \"Auth > Login (Admin)\" to populate {{adminToken}}.\n4. Run \"Admin > Create Course\" to capture {{courseId}}, {{lessonId}}, and {{batchId}}, or set them manually.\n5. Run \"Users > Get All Users\" to capture {{targetUserId}} for admin user actions.\n\nNotes:\n- Admin folders require an admin JWT.\n- Login is split into student/admin requests so both tokens can be kept at once.\n- Some known backend quirks are documented in the relevant request descriptions.",
